** ============================================================
** CONTACT INTERACTIONS
** ============================================================
**
*Surface Interaction, name="steel concrete"
** Hard contact in the normal direction
*Surface Behavior, DIRECT, pressure-overclosure=HARD
** Define surface-to-surface contact pair
*Contact Pair, interaction="steel concrete", type=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.PLATE_BOTTOM, concrete-1.CONCRETE_TOP
**
** ------------------------------------------------------------
** Steel-on-steel hard contact, same behaviour as above
** ------------------------------------------------------------
** Only one steel-on-steel pair remains: anchor shaft <-> plate hole, where the
** bearing pressure builds up across the 0.5 mm radial clearance of the d+1 hole.
** The washer/plate pair that used to sit here is now the WASHER_TO_PLATE tie.
** Slave (first) is the smaller / more finely meshed surface.
** Default FINITE sliding is used (not small sliding): the contact point on the
** shaft is free to migrate around the hole as the pair loads up.
*Surface Interaction, name="steel steel"
*Surface Behavior, DIRECT, pressure-overclosure=HARD
*Contact Pair, interaction="steel steel", type=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.ANCHOR_TO_PLATE, steel-1.PLATE_TO_ANCHOR
